      <title>The PGA Tour Should Welcome Prodigal Son Jon Rahm Home After LIV Exit</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-10-10/the-pga-tour-should-welcome-prodigal-son-jon-rahm-home-after-liv-exit</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">59ee252bddda57830d9a9fe6</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:02 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Three years ago, Jon Rahm was on top of the golf world. He had two major championships, a stint as the No. 1-ranked player in the world and star power. LIV, the Saudi-backed upstart challenging the PGA Tour, noticed. It needed a superstar to boost its credibility, and Rahm was the obvious prize. For a deal reportedly worth over $300 million, LIV lured him away.</description>
